  "not_observable": [
    {
      "case": "tests/unit/test_jobs.py::test_concurrent_claims_never_duplicate: six separate JobQueue handles race in six Python threads; the runner drives one worker process with --concurrency 6, so only the outcome (40 completed, none failed, none left queued) is observed, not the claim interleaving",
      "covered_by": "CORE-19"
    },
    {
      "case": "tests/unit/test_jobs.py::test_resource_limits: the gpu and repo resource keys cannot be set through `job enqueue` (it takes no resource_keys), and the services that set them need a classification or git sync run; the per-resource capacity from config jobs.gpu_concurrency is not reachable from a step",
      "covered_by": "CORE-19"
    },
    {
      "case": "tests/unit/test_jobs.py::test_verify_keys_are_bounded_by_verify_concurrency: the verify:<repository> keys are set by the verification service when a task is verified, and the claim order is asserted between queued jobs held by two verifications; no step enqueues verify jobs with keys nor holds a claim while another claim is attempted",
      "covered_by": "CORE-19"
    }
  ]
